The global module fragment allows a module to include traditional header files (e.g., `<iostream>`, `<vector>`) whose declarations are processed *before* the module's own declarations. It's initiated by `module;` followed by `#include` directives.
```cpp
module;
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>

export module MyModule; // Module declarations begin here
// ...
```
